   vibe:'Three neighbourhoods wearing one trench coat. Midtown Village (11th to Broad, Market to Locust) is the restaurant-row bit: 13th Street is Philly\'s attempt at a Soho dining strip, and about 60% of it works (Barbuzzo, Double Knot, El Vez, Sampan, Charlie was a Sinner) while 40% is Instagram bait with queues (Green Eggs, the brunch places). The Gayborhood (roughly 11th to 13th, Walnut to Pine, rainbow crosswalks) is the real, old, lived-in gay district: Woody\'s, Tavern on Camac\'s upstairs piano bar, Giovanni\'s Room bookshop, and it is the reason the neighbourhood is safe and awake at 1am. South of Locust it goes residential and pretty fast: Spruce, Pine and Delancey between 9th and 13th are brownstones, Antique Row is Pine, and Washington Square itself is a proper leafy square with almost nobody in it. Jefferson hospital and the students give the eastern half a slightly institutional feel; the northern edge (Chestnut/Market) is chains and a bit grubby.',
